a4_pointcloud_registration,A4 — 点云配准与非刚性形状匹配 (Point Cloud Registration & Non-Rigid Shape Matching),Gromov-Wasserstein point cloud shape matching ICML NeurIPS 2024 2025,5,Multi-Prototype Hyperbolic Learning Guided by Class Hierarchy | International Journal of Computer Vision | Springer Nature Link,https://link.springer.com/article/10.1007/s11263-025-02571-8,link.springer.com,0.9943141,"The Gromov-Wasserstein problem seeks to assign points \((x\_i)\_i\) to points \((y\_j)\_j\) so that their inner distances match as much as possible. Its formulation enables source points masses to be split and assigned to several target points, leading to a potential soft assignment P. Nonetheless, whenever the two empirical distributions are uniform with the same number of Diracs, and when \(M\_1\) and \(M\_2\) are both conditionally negative definite (CND), the optimal coupling P can be chosen as a permutation matrix, i.e. a one to one assignment (see Theorems 2 and 3, Sejourne et al. (2021. The unbalanced gromov wasserstein distance: Conic formulation and relaxation. In: Ranzato, M., Beygelzimer, A., Dauphin, Y., Liang, P.S., Vaughan, J.W. (eds.) Advances in Neural Information [...] Fig. 4

Illustration of the Gromov-Wasserstein assignment. The assignment is done in order to preserve ""as much as possible"" the distances. Its formulation enables a point to be split and assigned to several points from the other distribution. But in general, when the numbers of points in each side are equal and that the masses are uniformly distributed, each point is assigned a unique other point. [...] Garnot and Landrieu (2020. Leveraging class hierarchies with metric-guided prototype learning. arXiv preprint 
