# Robust Explanations of Graph Neural Networks via Graph Curvatures

### Abstract [...] Explaining graph neural networks (GNNs) is a key approach to improve the trustworthiness of GNN in high-stakes applications, such as finance and healthcare. However, existing methods are vulnerable to perturbations, raising concerns about explanation reliability. Prior methods enhance explanation robustness using model retraining or explanation ensemble, with certain weaknesses. Retraining leads to models that are different from the original target model and misleading explanations, while ensemble can produce contradictory results due to different inputs or models. To improve explanation robustness without the above weaknesses, we take an unexplored route and exploit the two edge geometry properties curvature and resistance to enhance explanation robustness. We are the first to prove that",True
