a1_keypoint_matching,A1 — 稀疏对应: 关键点匹配与特征对齐 (Sparse Correspondence: Keypoint Matching),visual correspondences keypoint detection Lie group alignment 2024 2025,3,Chapter 0 Abstract,https://arxiv.org/html/2604.09639v1,arxiv.org,0.18016468,"Given two images of the same scene with sufficient overlap, a local feature pipeline detects keypoints and computes descriptors, producing tentative correspondences
ℳ={(xkA,xkB)}k=1K\mathcal{M}=\{(x^{A}\_{k},x^{B}\_{k})\}\_{k=1}^{K}.
Such correspondences are a cornerstone of multi-view geometry: they enable robust estimation of epipolar relations and camera motion (often with RANSAC for outlier rejection), and they are the basic “glue” behind SfM/SLAM systems that triangulate and refine 3D structure from multi-view observations [lowe2004distinctive, fischler1981random, schonberger2016structure]. [...] In the context of stylization, correspondences become equally important as a consistency signal: if xkAx^{A}\_{k} and xkBx^{B}\_{k} observe the same physical point, the stylized appearance around these locations should remain compatible, otherwise downstream 3D reconstruction can lose track due to unstable visual evidence across views. [...] ###### Related learned correspondence families.

The broader literature includes detector-free matchers that directly predict dense/semidense correspondences, such as LoFTR[sun2021loftr], which replaces explicit keypoint detection with transformer-based coarse-to-fine matching and can be strong in low-texture regimes.
More recent work such as LightGlue[lindenberger2023lightglue] focuses on making learned matching efficient and scalable while retaining SuperGlue-like context reasoning.
These developments reinforce an important theme: multi-view consistency objectives benefit disproportionately from correspondence quality, and modern learned matchers often outperform classical heuristics when scenes include repeated patterns, motion blur, or challenging viewpoint changes.",True
a3_deep_matching,A3 — 深度匹配: 端到端对应学习 (Deep Feature Matching & End-to-End Correspondence),cost volume correlation layer optical flow learning theory 2024 2025,7,NeurIPS Poster High-Order Flow Matching: Unified Framework and Sharp Statistical Rates,https://neurips.cc/virtual/2025/poster/116548,neurips.cc,0.18010665,"Flow matching is an emerging generative modeling framework that learns continuous-time dynamics to map noise into data. To enhance expressiveness and sampling efficiency, recent works have explored incorporating high-order trajectory information. Despite the empirical success, a holistic theoretical foundation is still lacking. We present a unified framework for standard and high-order flow matching that incorporates trajectory derivatives up to an arbitrary order $K$. Our key innovation is establishing the marginalization technique that converts the intractable $K$-order loss into a simple conditional regression with exact gradients and identifying the consistency constraint. We establish sharp statistical rates of the $K$-order flow matching implemented with transformer networks. With [...] flow matching implemented with transformer networks. With $n$ samples, flow matching estimates nonparametric distributions at a rate $\tilde{O}(n^{-\Theta(1/d )})$, matching minimax lower bounds up to logarithmic factors. [...] Skip to yearly menu bar

