a4_pointcloud_registration,A4 — 点云配准与非刚性形状匹配 (Point Cloud Registration & Non-Rigid Shape Matching),ICP robust variant optimal transport registration 2024 2025 theory,4,Learning Point Correspondences In Radar 3D Point Clouds For Radar-Inertial Odometry,https://arxiv.org/html/2506.18580v1,arxiv.org,0.16238004,"Closest Point (ICP) or Normal Distribution Transform (NDT) cannot readily be applied to radar point clouds . Because of the challenging nature of the radar 3D point clouds there is a need for new methods to process them in state estimation pipelines. [...] Using the 3D point information in state estimation usually involves finding correspondences between points in subsequent point clouds. FMCW SoC radar point clouds are much different from their LiDAR counterparts in that they are orders of magnitude sparser which makes it impossible to sense structures in the environment . Moreover, they exhibit temporal and viewpoint variations, that is, point clouds of the same object measured in different time instants as well as point clouds of the same object but measured from slightly different viewpoints may differ very significantly . Additionally, they contain ghost reflections caused by speckle noise and multi-path reflections . Hence, classic techniques developed for LiDAR data, like Iterative Closest Point (ICP) or Normal Distribution Transform [...] Deep learning framework for predicting robust correspondences in sparse and noisy FMCW SoC radar 3D point clouds.

Efficient, self-supervised method not requiring hand-annotated ground-truth data.

Formulation of the learning problem as multi-label classification which allows training on the sparse and noisy 3D point clouds yet results in unambiguous matches.

Evaluation of the method with real-world data (our own dataset and a public benchmark Coloradar dataset ) in a state-of-the-art open-source RIO estimation framework.

Open-source implementation of the presented architecture together with the used dataset for the benefit of the research community.",True
