a1_keypoint_matching,A1 — 稀疏对应: 关键点匹配与特征对齐 (Sparse Correspondence: Keypoint Matching),feature matching correspondence field learning mathematical model 2024 2025,8,MatRes: Zero-Shot Test-Time Model Adaptation for Simultaneous Matching and Restoration,https://arxiv.org/html/2604.10081v1,arxiv.org,0.13898711,"### 3.2 Mutual Guidance

Recent studies [55, 70, 9, 50] have revealed that large-scale matching models ℳϕ\mathcal{M}\_{\phi} exhibit surprisingly strong emergent correspondence properties which can act as a generative prior.
In particular, features extracted from such models can enable accurate nearest-neighbor matching even without task-specific supervision.
These generative features are learned from large and diverse datasets, and thus often generalize well to unseen domains . [...] Restoration and matching methods
MatRes is compatible with any pretrained matching model where a gridwise feature map is computed, from which the geometric transform, most commonly in a deformation field format, in generated.
This includes recent deep learning–based correspondence methods such as LoftUp , ART ,
DIFT , RoMa , and Mast3R .
Similarly, any restoration model equipped with an encoder that produces gridwise feature representations and a decoder that reconstructs the restored image is compatible with MatRes.
This covers virtually all modern restoration architectures, including general-purpose models such as Restomer  and SwinIR , as well as task-specific methods for super-resolution, denoising, and deblurring, such as EDSR , N2N , N2V , DeblurGAN , and SRN .

Refer to caption [...] In this paper, we denote the denoised latent diffusion feature zt−1z\_{t-1} as z=ℳθ​(ℐ)z=\mathcal{M}\_{\theta}(\mathcal{I}), where ℐ\mathcal{I} is the input image.
Following prior works [55, 70, 9, 50], the denoised latent feature zz can be utilized for correspondence search, as it captures high-level semantic information while preserving local structural details.
Even without explicit supervision, these features naturally exhibit correspondence-friendly behavior, allowing reliable estimation through nearest-neighbor matching in the feature space.

